Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: fan and keyboard backlight control for Gigabyte G5/G6 laptops
 GigaControl gives Gigabyte G-series gaming laptops the fan and RGB keyboard
 control their firmware keeps to itself: fan profiles and editable custom
 curves, backlight colour and brightness that survive a reboot and a suspend,
 and live temperature and RPM readings.
 .
 A small root daemon owns Embedded Controller access and exposes it on the D-Bus
 system bus, authorising each write through polkit — the console user changes
 fan speed or backlight colour without a password, as with screen brightness.
 The desktop app and the command line tools are unprivileged clients of it.
 .
 These laptops are Clevo-ODM designs whose EC speaks a Clevo-style mailbox
 protocol, reverse engineered and verified on a Gigabyte G6 KF. Installation is
 refused on hardware outside the G5/G6/G7 range, and every write is read back.
 .
 On GNOME the tray indicator needs an AppIndicator extension, which Ubuntu
 preinstalls; without one the app runs from its window alone.
